# PyInstaller
#  Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#  before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec
#  ...but packaging/rpm/ash.spec is a tracked source file, not a PyInstaller artifact.
#  This rule already cost the project the rpm spec once: it was written, verified
#  against, and never landed, because `git add <dir>` skips ignored files silently
#  instead of failing. packaging/rpm/build.sh then referenced a file no clean checkout
#  had, and the rpm: CI job could not pass. Keep this negation next to the rule it
#  narrows, so a future rpm spec does not disappear the same way.
!packaging/rpm/ash.spec

